module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersion.IdealSheafKer
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersion.RingedSpaceComorphism

/-!
# From a closed immersion of schemes to a closed immersion of ringed spaces

`AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion` is a property of a morphism of schemes;
`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.IsClosedImmersion` ([Stacks Project, Tag 01C2]) is the Stacks Project's
notion for a morphism of ringed spaces. The second is what the conormal-sheaf constructions of
[Stacks Project, Tag 01R1] and [Stacks Project, Tag 01R2] consume, and nothing derived it from
the first.

This file discharges two of its three conditions and isolates the third.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.epi_structureSheafModuleHom` : the structure-sheaf map of a closed
  immersion of schemes is an epimorphism of sheaves of modules on the underlying ringed space.
* `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.isClosedImmersion_toShHom` : a closed immersion of schemes underlies a
  closed immersion of ringed spaces, given local generation of its ideal sheaf by sections.

## Implementation notes

The closed-embedding condition is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion.isClosedEmbedding`
transported along the forgetful functors, which leave the base map untouched.

The surjectivity condition is stated by `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.IsClosedImmersion` as an
epimorphism in `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing X)`, whereas what
`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.isLocallySurjective_c_toShHom` supplies is local surjectivity of the
comorphism of structure sheaves, a morphism of sheaves of *commutative rings*. The two are
connected by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective` together with the
observation that the image sieves coincide: `TopCat.Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective` is by
definition `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective` for `Opens.grothendieckTopology`, and
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.imageSieve` depends only on the underlying functions on sections, which
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit_val_app_apply` makes literally the same.
So the sieve membership transfers with no construction at all.

What remains is the local-generation condition, `Nonempty (LocalGeneratorsData (idealSheaf i))`:
quasi-coherence of the ideal sheaf, [Stacks Project, Tag 01IN] at the sheaf level. Its
section-level content is available —
`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.range_idealSheafι_val_app_eq_map_of_le` says that over affine opens
`U ≤ V` the sections of the ideal sheaf over `U` are generated by the restrictions of those over
`V`, which is exactly the generation statement a `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`
of `(idealSheaf i).over V` asserts. Turning it into that structure is the step not taken here: it
has to be run through `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.free`,
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv` and `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.over` on the
slice site `(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).over V`, and so is a statement about the over-category
machinery rather than about ideal sheaves.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01IN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01R2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01R2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction 

universe u

namespace Stacks.ClosedImmersion

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X) [AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion f]

/-- **The structure-sheaf map of a closed immersion of schemes is an epimorphism of sheaves of
modules.** This is the surjectivity condition of [Stacks Project, Tag 01C2] for the underlying
morphism of ringed spaces.

`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.isLocallySurjective_c_toShHom` gives local surjectivity of the
comorphism of structure sheaves, and the image sieve of a morphism of presheaves depends only on
the underlying functions on sections, which are the same for the comorphism and for the induced
morphism of sheaves of modules. -/
theorem epi_structureSheafModuleHom : Epi (structureSheafModuleHom f.toLRSHom.toShHom) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _
    ⟨fun s ↦ (isLocallySurjective_c_toShHom f).imageSieve_mem s⟩

/-- **A closed immersion of schemes underlies a closed immersion of ringed spaces**, once its
ideal sheaf is known to be locally generated by sections.

The closed-embedding condition is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion.isClosedEmbedding` and the
surjectivity condition is `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.epi_structureSheafModuleHom`; only the
local-generation hypothesis is left to the caller. It is quasi-coherence of the ideal sheaf, whose
section-level content is `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.range_idealSheafι_val_app_eq_map_of_le`; see the
module docstring. -/
theorem isClosedImmersion_toShHom (hgen : Nonempty (SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData.{u}
    (idealSheaf f.toLRSHom.toShHom))) :
    IsClosedImmersion f.toLRSHom.toShHom where
  isClosedEmbedding := AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion.isClosedEmbedding f
  structureSheafMap_epi := epi_structureSheafModuleHom f
  kernel_locallyGenerated := hgen

end Stacks.ClosedImmersion

end
